BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-paye-payment@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261022
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261023
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=22
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: PAYE and National Insurance payment to HMRC (monthl
 y)
DESCRIPTION:Pay what you owe by the 22nd of the month (or the 19th if payin
 g by post). The amount is the tax and National Insurance reported on your 
 FPS in the previous tax month\, minus any EPS reductions.\nApplies to: Emp
 loyers paying HMRC monthly (other than by cheque through the post)\nNon-wo
 rking-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/running-pa
 yroll/paying-hmrc\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.ht
 ml#united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates
  follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays ar
 e not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-paye-payment-post@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=19
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: PAYE and National Insurance payment to HMRC by post
  (cheque)
DESCRIPTION:If you pay by cheque through the post\, it must reach HMRC by t
 he 19th of the month.\nApplies to: Employers paying HMRC by cheque through
  the post\nNon-working-day rule: check the source.\n\nSource: https://www.
 gov.uk/pay-paye-tax\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.
 html#united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dat
 es follow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays 
 are not applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-paye-eps@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20261019
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20261020
RRULE:FREQ=MONTHLY;BYMONTHDAY=19
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Employer Payment Summary (EPS) to claim reductions
DESCRIPTION:In the next tax month (which starts on the 6th)\, you can claim
  any reduction on what you'll owe HMRC (for example statutory pay) by send
 ing an Employer Payment Summary (EPS) by the 19th.\nApplies to: Employers 
 claiming reductions such as statutory pay\nNon-working-day rule: check the
  source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/running-payroll/reporting-to-hmrc\n
 Details: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom\n
 \nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurri
 ng rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sour
 ces last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:uk-p60@intelligentpayroll.eu
DTSTAMP:20261006T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270531
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270601
RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=5;BYMONTHDAY=31
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Give employees a P60
DESCRIPTION:Give your employees a P60 by 31 May (for the tax year ending 5 
 April).\nApplies to: Employers running payroll\nNon-working-day rule: chec
 k the source.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/payroll-annual-reporting\nDeta
 ils: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom\n\nFo
 r information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates follow the recurring r
 ule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are not applied. Sources 
 last checked 4 October 2026.
URL:https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#united-kingdom
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
