RRULE:FREQ=YEARLY;BYMONTH=7;BYMONTHDAY=22
SUMMARY:United Kingdom: Class 1A National Insurance payment on benefits
DESCRIPTION:Your Class 1A National Insurance payment must be received by 22
  July (or 19 July if you're paying by post).\nApplies to: Employers that p
 rovided taxable expenses and benefits\nNon-working-day rule: check the sou
 rce.\n\nSource: https://www.gov.uk/payroll-annual-reporting/report-expense
 s-and-benefits\nDetails: https://www.intelligentpayroll.eu/deadlines.html#
 united-kingdom\n\nFor information only\, not legal or tax advice. Dates fo
 llow the recurring rule stated by the source\; weekends and holidays are n
 ot applied. Sources last checked 4 October 2026.
